68
00:06:25.886 --> 00:06:28.276
Pocket change.

69
00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:30.891
Whoa.

70
00:06:31.016 --> 00:06:33.323
Uh. yeah.
That was the band's name.

71
00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.393
Gotcha.

72
00:06:34.477 --> 00:06:36.062
Can I get you a beer?

73
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.745
Yeah. Absolutely.

74
00:06:38.815 --> 00:06:39.664
Yeah.

75
00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:41.192
- See ya.
- Be right back. Yeah.

76
00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:43.834
So I was in LA for a few years.

77
00:06:43.904 --> 00:06:47.295
and I was with some promising bands.
but they never took off.

78
00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:50.702
And eventually I just got worn out
from the grind.

79
00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:53.455
It's funny. though.
I don't miss it.

80
00:06:54.623 --> 00:06:55.513
Really?

81
00:06:55.583 --> 00:06:56.680
Yeah.

82
00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.306
Man. gotta say. it's weird seeing you

83
00:06:58.376 --> 00:07:00.128
wind up in the corporate world.

84
00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:02.060
Yeah. that's what I thought.

85
00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.353
But this company I'm with.

86
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.147
it's. like.
a perfect fit for people like us.

87
00:07:06.217 --> 00:07:09.971
Smart. creative types
with unrealized ambition

88
00:07:10.055 --> 00:07:12.390
who just don't know
what they're doing with their lives.

89
00:07:12.641 --> 00:07:13.641
Okay.

90
00:07:14.184 --> 00:07:17.409
And I'm a lot happier knowing
I don't have to scramble for gigs

91
00:07:17.479 --> 00:07:19.522
just to make rent every month.

92
00:07:20.148 --> 00:07:23.902
And the whole frustration
with not making it in music.

93
00:07:23.985 --> 00:07:26.112
that's all gone.

94
00:07:27.489 --> 00:07:29.866
Well. hey. man.
I'm happy for you.

95
00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.965
We're always looking for new people.

96
00:07:32.035 --> 00:07:33.119
Oh.

97
00:07:33.328 --> 00:07:35.622
I can put in a good word for you.

98
00:07:37.415 --> 00:07:39.209
Uh. what's the pay like?

99
00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:42.045
Entry level starts at 100K.

100
