No experience required.

101
00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:48.593
Mm-hmm.

102
00:07:48.802 --> 00:07:49.774
It's good to see you. Luke.

103
00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:51.805
Yeah. yeah. You too.

104
00:07:52.097 --> 00:07:53.682
Think about it.

105
00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:08.530
Babe. are you coming to bed soon?

106
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.949
Yeah. as soon as I finish this.

107
00:08:11.908 --> 00:08:13.924
Luke. I've got to be up in five hours.

108
00:08:13.994 --> 00:08:16.079
Yeah. I'll be quick.

109
00:08:19.082 --> 00:08:22.544
Do you think you'll follow up
with Andy about that job?

110
00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:27.048
Uh. is this your way of telling me
you think I should?

111
00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:31.566
I don't know.
it just sounded like a good opportunity.

112
00:08:31.636 --> 00:08:33.013
don't you think?

113
00:08:34.139 --> 00:08:36.808
And what about my music?

114
00:08:37.058 --> 00:08:39.269
You could still do it on the side.

115
00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.160
How much drawing have you done

116
00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:45.191
since you started working at the lab?

117
00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:48.959
I'm gonna get back to it soon. okay?

118
00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:51.573
Yeah. You've been saying that for years.

119
00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:54.381
I haven't really had the time. you know.

120
00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:58.301
But my job is what lets me
afford this apartment.

121
00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:03.251
which you seem to be enjoying
more than yours right now.

122
00:09:04.627 --> 00:09:05.670
Okay.

123
00:09:06.129 --> 00:09:09.020
I'm sorry. I just...
I think I'm in a bad mood

124
00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:12.273
from the record label guy flaking. okay?

125
00:09:12.343 --> 00:09:15.305
Okay.
It's not just tonight. though. is it?

126
00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:16.806
What do you mean?

127
00:09:18.141 --> 00:09:21.199
Look. I get that music is your dream.

128
00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:25.161
but it doesn't seem to make you happy.

129
00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:27.650
It really just makes you
hard to be around.

130
00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:33.323
I can't help it that
I want more out of life than...

131
00:09:34.115 --> 00:09:35.241
this.

132
00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:38.787
This?

133
00:09:39.954 --> 00:09:42.637
I'm sorry.
Do you have any idea how hurtful

134
00:09:42.707 --> 00:09:44.250
that is to say to me?

135
00:09:44.626 --> 00:09:46.307
I didn't mean you. obviously.

136
00:09:46.377 --> 00:09:49.255
No. it's not obvious. Luke.

137
00:09:51.257 --> 00:09:55.929
You know. I think I need a break
from you right now.

138
00:09:56.346 --> 00:09:58.723
I think you should go back
to your place.

139
00:09:59.974 --> 00:10:03.520
Come on. Let's just...
Let's talk about this. okay?

140
00:10:03.978 --> 00:10:05.105
EI!

141
00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:14.114
Fuck. Fuck.

142
00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:40.056
Okay.

143
00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:08.751
Fuck.

144
00:11:36.946 --> 00:11:38.670
- Hi. Welcome.
- Hey.

145
00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:40.922
Welcome to the team.
It's so nice to meet you.

146
00:11:40.992 --> 00:11:42.340
Thank you. Nice to meet you as well.

147
00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.259
Have a look around if you'd like.

148
00:11:44.329 --> 00:11:45.052
Wow.

149
00:11:45.122 --> 00:11:47.804
Can I grab you anything?
Water? Kombucha?

150
00:11:47.874 --> 00:11:49.792
I'm good. but thank you.

151
00:11:51.169 --> 00:11:53.351
Someone will be with you shortly.

152
00:11:53.421 --> 00:11:54.839
Sounds good.

153
00:12:03.806 --> 00:12:06.489
"Success starts
with a symbiotic culture.

154
00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:11.105
like our original SCOOBY
for our designer kombucha.”

155
00:12:12.941 --> 00:12:15.165
Ugh. It's like living mucus.

156
00:12:15.235 --> 00:12:16.791
She's beautiful. isn't she?

157
00:12:16.861 --> 00:12:19.002
Uh. yeah. you could say that.

158
00:12:19.072 --> 00:12:22.005
You know. legend has it
she's descended from a SCOOBY

159
00:12:22.075 --> 00:12:25.954
the Dalai Lama gave Jesuit missionaries
over 300 years ago.

160
00:12:26.204 --> 00:12:29.095
Or maybe the Jesuits
stole it from the Dalai Lama.

161
00:12:29.165 --> 00:12:30.430
I can never remember.

162
00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.641
Kelsey Rhodes. managing director
of our consulting team.

163
00:12:33.711 --> 00:12:35.435
Luke Merritt. Nice to meet you.

164
00:12:35.505 --> 00:12:36.589
Shall we?

165
00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:38.007
Yeah.

166
00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:41.636
So. this is our space.

167
00:12:47.725 --> 00:12:49.185
Thank you.

168
00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.033
Please. sit.

169
00:13:04.158 --> 00:13:05.158
Yeah.

170
00:13:08.246 --> 00:13:11.304
We are so thrilled
to have you join the Symbio team.

171
00:13:11.374 --> 00:13:13.876
Oh. wait. I thought...

172
00:13:14.002 --> 00:13:15.808
Don't I have to. like. interview?

173
00:13:15.878 --> 00:13:18.423
Andy's recommendation is enough for me.

174
00:13:18.548 --> 00:13:20.730
We like to start
with a one-month probationary period.

175
00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.317
but candidates with referrals
almost always blend right in.

176
00:13:24.387 --> 00:13:27.765
You can start today.
assuming that our terms

177
00:13:28.433 --> 00:13:30.059
are to your approval.

178
00:13:31.394 --> 00:13:34.272
Uh. yeah. Wow. that's...

179
00:13:34.397 --> 00:13:35.745
This is amazing.

180
00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:38.151
Excellent.
We can finish the paperwork later.

181
00:13:38.234 --> 00:13:41.446
Now. how much has Andy
told you about what we do here?

182
00:13:41.529 --> 00:13:43.127
Uh. not much.

183
00:13:43.197 --> 00:13:46.214
He just said this is a great place
for the smart.

184
00:13:46.284 --> 00:13:47.091
creative type.

185
00:13:47.161 --> 00:13:50.843
Mhm. One of the great tragedies
of our time is how

186
00:13:50.913 --> 00:13:54.138
the underemployed liberal arts majors
are toiling away

187
00:13:54.208 --> 00:13:57.267
in menial jobs.
distracted by dreams of stardom.

188
00:13:57.337 --> 00:14:00.520
when they really have
no chance of success.

189
00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:01.646
Meanwhile. the corporate world

190
00:14:01.716 --> 00:14:03.982
is run by finance
and engineering majors

191
00:14:04.052 --> 00:14:07.568
with zero imagination or empathy.

192
00:14:07.638 --> 00:14:10.780
But we've cracked the code
on how creatives can thrive

193
00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.783
and inject new life
into stagnant businesses.

194
00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:15.660
And we practice what we preach.

195
00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:19.247
Okay. so what exactly will I be doing?

196
00:14:19.317 --> 00:14:21.958
As a culture consultant.
you'll diagnose the deficiencies

197
00:14:22.028 --> 00:14:24.043
in our clients' existing cultures.

198
00:14:24.113 --> 00:14:27.130
Then you'll prescribe a blend
of our proprietary work rituals

199
00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.507
to suit their needs and. of course.

200
00:14:29.577 --> 00:14:31.537
sell them on our secret weapon.

201
00:14:32.455 --> 00:14:33.469
Secret weapon?

202
00:14:33.539 --> 00:14:34.762
You've already seen it.

203
00:14:34.832 --> 00:14:36.764
Our in-house. designer kombucha.

204
00:14:36.834 --> 00:14:39.934
which started as someone's fun
side project until we realized

205
00:14:40.004 --> 00:14:42.507
the incredible benefits.

206
00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:43.688
Imagine:

207
00:14:43.758 --> 00:14:47.317
Every employee working
with peak energy and laser focus.

208
00:14:47.387 --> 00:14:48.985
with no jitters or crashing.

209
00:14:49.055 --> 00:14:51.946
Their gut biome and body chemistry
perfectly synced

210
00:14:52.016 --> 00:14:55.199
from drinking kombucha
designed just for their company.

211
00:14:55.269 --> 00:15:00.038
Team unity at a cellular level.
a true symbiosis

212
00:15:00.108 --> 00:15:03.027
between employees
and their organization...

213
00:15:03.736 --> 00:15:06.114
No matter what major
they had in college.

214
00:15:06.989 --> 00:15:08.950
But what if they don't like kombucha?

215
00:15:09.075 --> 00:15:09.965
Believe it or not.

216
00:15:10.035 --> 00:15:12.342
we've never run
into that problem before.

217
00:15:12.412 --> 00:15:14.385
Everybody gets on board eventually.

218
00:15:14.455 --> 00:15:15.887
Do you partake?

219
00:15:15.957 --> 00:15:17.959
I don't. Uh...

220
00:15:18.167 --> 00:15:21.100
Those floating SCOBY things
kind of freak me out.

221
00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.894
Okay. well. don't worry.

222
00:15:22.964 --> 00:15:24.145
You'll get over that.

223
00:15:24.215 --> 00:15:25.730
Do you know what SCOOBY stands for?

224
00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:26.731
Uh. no.

225
00:15:26.801 --> 00:15:29.150
Symbiotic culture of bacteria and yeast.

226
00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:31.778
A natural. harmonious partnership.

227
00:15:31.848 --> 00:15:33.850
Really nothing to be afraid of.

228
00:15:34.851 --> 00:15:37.478
I think I'll stick with this.

229
00:15:38.104 --> 00:15:39.522
We'll see about that.

230
00:15:42.358 --> 00:15:44.082
So. this is your desk.

231
00:15:44.152 --> 00:15:45.792
Oop. Sorry.

232
00:15:45.862 --> 00:15:47.794
This was supposed to be cleared out.

233
00:15:52.161 --> 00:15:55.176
All yours.
Andy will be your on boarding buddy.

234
00:15:55.246 --> 00:15:57.874
and he can fill you in
on your first assignment. Andy?

235
00:15:57.957 --> 00:15:59.292
On it. boss.

236
00:16:00.209 --> 00:16:01.974
Ma'am. you can't be in here.

237
00:16:02.044 --> 00:16:04.380
No. I want to talk to her now.

238
00:16:05.882 --> 00:16:07.091
You...

239
00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:10.386
You killed my daughter.

240
00:16:12.013 --> 00:16:13.639
Excuse me.

241
00:16:14.515 --> 00:16:17.477
Hi. We need security
in the lobby right now.

242
00:16:21.731 --> 00:16:25.443
You. You're next.

243
00:16:26.652 --> 00:16:28.070
This place is cursed!

244
00:16:28.696 --> 00:16:30.948
Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

245
00:16:31.032 --> 00:16:32.380
Get out while you still can!

246
00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:33.298
Okay. That's enough.

247
00:16:33.368 --> 00:16:35.369
Don't touch me!

248
00:16:37.705 --> 00:16:38.512
Man.

249
00:16:38.582 --> 00:16:41.848
Downtown just keeps getting
crazier and crazier. huh?

250
00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:42.627
Yeah.

251
00:16:42.752 --> 00:16:45.129
Let's get you started
on this pitch deck.

252
00:17:11.322 --> 00:17:12.573
Oh.

253
00:17:16.911 --> 00:17:19.664
Okay.

254
00:17:30.007 --> 00:17:32.482
Calling without a text first.
That's bold.

255
00:17:32.552 --> 00:17:34.233
I wanted to hear your voice.

256
00:17:34.303 --> 00:17:36.097
And to tell you.

257
00:17:36.597 --> 00:17:39.225
I decided to take the job
at Andy's company.

258
00:17:39.475 --> 00:17:41.936
Oh. You did?

259
00:17:42.144 --> 00:17:43.145
Yeah.

260
00:17:43.271 --> 00:17:44.077
Wow.

261
00:17:44.147 --> 00:17:45.953
Is that a good wow?

262
00:17:46.023 --> 00:17:49.026
Like we should celebrate tonight wow?

263
00:17:50.528 --> 00:17:53.044
I'm really happy for you.

264
00:17:53.114 --> 00:17:57.577
I just need some time
